From: PupJune2 <PupJune2@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 16:00:00 +0000
Subject: CromIKO Secure DNS

Add providers to the secure DNS (DNS-over-HTTPS) list in Settings >
Privacy > Use secure DNS, and make Quad9 the default:

- AdGuard: ad blocking, family protection and unfiltered.
- dnsforge.de: ad blocking, family filter and unfiltered.
- Mullvad: unfiltered and ad blocking.
- Quad9 (9.9.9.9) is listed again (Chromium turned it off).
- Cloudflare (1.1.1.1), Google (Public DNS) and the others stay.

Quad9 (a Swiss non-profit that blocks malware domains) is now the
default provider, instead of OpenDNS when no provider is chosen. Like
in Cromite, secure DNS is on by default.

The addresses and DoH templates are from the providers' own pages, and
each template answers DNS queries.

